# Inline layout limit 31 launch review

**Verdict: APPROVE this exact prospective JS→Native batch, with Native conditional on the complete JS oracle pass.** No compiler or consumer was run.

The patch (`7368bc1c8cce34ebb7e6b164c9ae254ef2ae12a6253c31a6e95959d073a2f312`) makes only two changes from graph845: it adds `INLINE_LAYOUT_LIMIT = 31` and uses it in `lay_of`'s final inline-layout size test. `WIDE = 247`, `lay_node`, constructor CID encoding, and the physical arity paths are unchanged. The existing `val_to` routing handles differing layouts through `val_box`, `val_unbox`, or `val_arms`; boxing/unboxing rebuilds and reads fields using `lay_node`. This affects ownership-bearing representations, so it is a bounded experiment, not a universal affine/runtime proof.

The JS and Native plans (`71dea9b963b4231c566462dcd5b43ae5b25a8c2856d9f284bd8ea7837fd31742`, `57429e883e319b090d1e93189c8b8fe92f6a73267e9dfe38094992c0b68ea89b`), FREEZE (`51f6a4f5370d9ff470a61a205573672f75368ac6647218e31d581d2b53060663`), and LAUNCH (`1998b5ac3e17cf9c165e02e97397f33666b5b7cdbd0ec2cc99e6c0b2bfa1487b`) join. All 136 pins and six resource-root inventories match. Both roles bind the same 53-file Unit source and 207,834-byte oracle (SHA256 `14565a3635124edb3ba8ef53b76e2030c3b3698e5d7c4a31989bc3ca9fb54a2d`). Fresh JS, generated C, Native binary, receipt, raw-stream, and guard paths are absent. Existing CPU 3 emit/build/consumer caps of 30/120/5 seconds, source guards, and full byte comparison remain bound; Native uses standard `-O3` without extra backend flags. No activation, performance claim, or adoption is included.
